Package: clip-keeper
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Arvind <arvindkumarsjpr@gmail.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, python3-cryptography, gir1.2-secret-1
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: private clipboard history for the GNOME top bar (copycat-compatible)
 Records what you copy (skipping password-manager secrets and anything that
 looks like a token or password), shows the latest clips in the top bar and
 opens a fuzzy-search popup on Super+V. Works on Wayland without a GNOME Shell
 extension, so GNOME upgrades do not break it. The history uses copycat's
 database format and location. Optional: full-text search, snippets on
 Super+Alt+3…9, paste transformed or edited, multi-select, file and rich-text
 copies, auto-expiry, and encryption at rest with the key in GNOME Keyring.
